--- This file defines the shared memory of Memory Reference Parameters, at the level of data:
--- a block of shared memory holds one list of data fragments (List{Data}, as the data
--- streams do), with no addresses or offsets.
---
--- The model follows the two views of [Client API] v1.0, section 3.2.5 (Synchronization): the
--- client's view of a block (cview of SharedMem) and the TA's view of one memory
--- reference (tview of MemrefOp), with two synchronizations.
---   1. When an operation starts (smcReq), each memory reference of the operation becomes a
---      MemrefOp mop(M, I), I the index of the parameter, whose tview is the client's data,
---      and the TA receives mref(mop(M, I)).
---   2. When the operation completes (smcRet), the tview of each MemrefOp of the client is
---      synchronized back to the client if the direction is output or input-output and the
---      final size is at most the original size ([Internal Core] v1.3.1, Table 4-9): the
---      client then sees the first size fragments.  A larger size is a request for a larger
---      buffer, and no data is synchronized.  The MemrefOp is removed, so the TA cannot
---      access the memory reference after the operation ([Internal Core] 4.3.6.4).
--- The memory references of a client are
---   * registered: memref(M, D), the whole block M (TEEC_MEMREF_WHOLE, or a
---     TEEC_MEMREF_PARTIAL_* type of direction D over the whole block);
---   * temporary: tmpref(X, Z, D), the client's buffer variable X with the size variable Z,
---     as in TEEC_TempMemoryReference.  The data of X are synchronized back to X and the
---     returned size to Z;
---   * null: nullref(Z, D), a temporary reference with no buffer.  The TA sees the size 0,
---     and the size it returns (the required size of an output) goes to Z.
--- A TA that calls another TA (TEE_InvokeTACommand) passes its temporary references the same
--- way, through reqInvoke and finishReqInvoke ([Internal Core] 4.9, Table 4-16).  A TA that
--- passes on a memory reference it received, mref(O), passes the same MemrefOp, so the two TAs
--- share it.
--- A well-behaved client does not access the memory while the reference is live ([Client
--- API] 3.2.5).  A rogue client can change it at any time ([Internal Core] 4.3, Security
--- Considerations): shm-tamper sets the tview to one of the alternatives in the tamper
--- attribute of the block.  An empty tamper (noAlt) is a well-behaved client.
---
--- Deviations from the specification:
---   * The parameters of a TA command are the typed parameters of its IMP function, with
---     the type TEE-Memref for a memory reference.  There is no paramTypes with four
---     TEE_Param slots, so a parameter type mismatch is not modeled.
---   * Partial memory references over a part of a block are not modeled: a part is a block
---     of its own.
---   * A read or write of the TA reads or writes the whole datum at once.  A memory
---     reference passed to an [inbuf] parameter of a TEE API is read once, when the
---     parameter is bound.  A memory reference cannot be passed to an [outbuf] parameter: the
---     TA writes the output to private memory and then to the memory reference.
---   * Only registered blocks have a rogue client; the client buffers of temporary
---     references do not change during the operation.
---   * A write to an input memory reference, and a write past the original size, are
---     programmer errors that the implementation need not detect ([Internal Core] 4.3.6.4).
---     The model panics the TA, so that they are detected.  So does an access after the
---     operation: the TA is stuck on it.
---   * A registered reference to a block of another client is stuck in the SMC request.

--- This module defines the IMP syntax of shared memory.
--- In a TA:
---   shmData(E): the data of the memory reference E (params[i].memref.buffer);
---   shmSize(E): its size (params[i].memref.size);
---   shmWrite(E, E'): writes the data E' to the memory reference E;
---   shmSetSize(E, E'): sets the size of E to E', the size returned to the client;
---   checkMemoryAccessRights(macc(R, W, A), E): TEE_CheckMemoryAccessRights with the flags
---     TEE_MEMORY_ACCESS_READ (R), _WRITE (W) and _ANY_OWNER (A) on the buffer E.
--- In a client (an RA):
---   shmAlloc(E, D): allocates a block of size E with the flags D (TEEC_AllocateSharedMemory);
---   shmFill(E, E'): writes the data E' to the block E;  shmView(E): the data of the block E;
---   shmRetSize(E): the size returned for the block E by the last operation;
---   shmRogue(E, E'): from now on, a rogue thread of the client may write E' to the block E
---     while it is shared;
---   shmRelease(E): releases the block E (TEEC_ReleaseSharedMemory);
---   memrefTo(E, D): a memory reference to the whole block E with direction D;
---   tmpref(X, Z, D), nullref(Z, D): temporary and null memory references;
---   teecInvoke(ES, EF, EL, OUT): TEEC_InvokeCommand of the command EF in the session ES with
---     the arguments EL; the output values are assigned to OUT.

--- @kind program
--- @feature shm
fmod SHARED-MEMORY-SYNTAX is
  pr IMP-STRICTNESS .

  sort MemrefDir .
  ops mrIn mrOut mrInout : -> MemrefDir [ctor] .
  sort MemAccess .
  op macc : Bool Bool Bool -> MemAccess [ctor] .

  ops shmData shmSize shmView shmRetSize shmRelease : Exp -> Exp [ctor] .
  ops shmWrite shmSetSize shmFill shmRogue : Exp Exp -> Exp [ctor] .
  ops shmAlloc memrefTo : Exp MemrefDir -> Exp [ctor] .
  op tmpref : Exp Exp MemrefDir -> Exp [ctor] .
  op nullref : Exp MemrefDir -> Exp [ctor] .
  op checkMemoryAccessRights : MemAccess Exp -> Exp [ctor] .
  op teecInvoke : Exp Exp ExpList ExpList -> Exp [ctor] .

  --- Contexts: $sh1(E) is the hole of a unary operator E, $sh2(E1, E2) the first operand
  --- of a binary one and $sh3(V, E2) the second.
  ops $sh1 : Exp -> KLabel [ctor] .
  op $sh2 : Exp Exp -> KLabel [ctor] .
  op $sh3 : Value Exp -> KLabel [ctor] .
  op $shTmp1 : Exp MemrefDir -> KLabel [ctor] .
  op $shTmp2 : Value MemrefDir -> KLabel [ctor] .
  op $shNull : MemrefDir -> KLabel [ctor] .
  op $shHole : -> Exp [ctor] .

  vars E E1 E2 Z : Exp .
  vars V V1 V2 : Value .
  var K : K .
  var D : MemrefDir .
  var MA : MemAccess .

  --- Strictness: the operands are evaluated left to right, as in IMP-STRICTNESS.  The
  --- operator waits in the context with $shHole in place of the operand.
  ceq k({ shmData(E) } ~> K) = k({ E } ~> $sh1(shmData($shHole)) ~> K) if not E :: Value .
  ceq k({ shmSize(E) } ~> K) = k({ E } ~> $sh1(shmSize($shHole)) ~> K) if not E :: Value .
  ceq k({ shmView(E) } ~> K) = k({ E } ~> $sh1(shmView($shHole)) ~> K) if not E :: Value .
  ceq k({ shmRetSize(E) } ~> K) = k({ E } ~> $sh1(shmRetSize($shHole)) ~> K) if not E :: Value .
  ceq k({ shmRelease(E) } ~> K) = k({ E } ~> $sh1(shmRelease($shHole)) ~> K) if not E :: Value .
  ceq k({ shmAlloc(E, D) } ~> K) = k({ E } ~> $sh1(shmAlloc($shHole, D)) ~> K) if not E :: Value .
  ceq k({ memrefTo(E, D) } ~> K) = k({ E } ~> $sh1(memrefTo($shHole, D)) ~> K) if not E :: Value .
  ceq k({ checkMemoryAccessRights(MA, E) } ~> K)
    = k({ E } ~> $sh1(checkMemoryAccessRights(MA, $shHole)) ~> K) if not E :: Value .
  eq k({ V } ~> $sh1(shmData($shHole)) ~> K) = k({ shmData(V) } ~> K) .
  eq k({ V } ~> $sh1(shmSize($shHole)) ~> K) = k({ shmSize(V) } ~> K) .
  eq k({ V } ~> $sh1(shmView($shHole)) ~> K) = k({ shmView(V) } ~> K) .
  eq k({ V } ~> $sh1(shmRetSize($shHole)) ~> K) = k({ shmRetSize(V) } ~> K) .
  eq k({ V } ~> $sh1(shmRelease($shHole)) ~> K) = k({ shmRelease(V) } ~> K) .
  eq k({ V } ~> $sh1(shmAlloc($shHole, D)) ~> K) = k({ shmAlloc(V, D) } ~> K) .
  eq k({ V } ~> $sh1(memrefTo($shHole, D)) ~> K) = k({ memrefTo(V, D) } ~> K) .
  eq k({ V } ~> $sh1(checkMemoryAccessRights(MA, $shHole)) ~> K)
    = k({ checkMemoryAccessRights(MA, V) } ~> K) .

  ceq k({ shmWrite(E1, E2) } ~> K) = k({ E1 } ~> $sh2(shmWrite($shHole, E2), E2) ~> K) if not E1 :: Value .
  ceq k({ shmSetSize(E1, E2) } ~> K) = k({ E1 } ~> $sh2(shmSetSize($shHole, E2), E2) ~> K) if not E1 :: Value .
  ceq k({ shmFill(E1, E2) } ~> K) = k({ E1 } ~> $sh2(shmFill($shHole, E2), E2) ~> K) if not E1 :: Value .
  ceq k({ shmRogue(E1, E2) } ~> K) = k({ E1 } ~> $sh2(shmRogue($shHole, E2), E2) ~> K) if not E1 :: Value .
  eq k({ V1 } ~> $sh2(shmWrite($shHole, E2), E2) ~> K) = k({ shmWrite(V1, E2) } ~> K) .
  eq k({ V1 } ~> $sh2(shmSetSize($shHole, E2), E2) ~> K) = k({ shmSetSize(V1, E2) } ~> K) .
  eq k({ V1 } ~> $sh2(shmFill($shHole, E2), E2) ~> K) = k({ shmFill(V1, E2) } ~> K) .
  eq k({ V1 } ~> $sh2(shmRogue($shHole, E2), E2) ~> K) = k({ shmRogue(V1, E2) } ~> K) .
  ceq k({ shmWrite(V1, E2) } ~> K) = k({ E2 } ~> $sh3(V1, shmWrite(V1, $shHole)) ~> K) if not E2 :: Value .
  ceq k({ shmSetSize(V1, E2) } ~> K) = k({ E2 } ~> $sh3(V1, shmSetSize(V1, $shHole)) ~> K) if not E2 :: Value .
  ceq k({ shmFill(V1, E2) } ~> K) = k({ E2 } ~> $sh3(V1, shmFill(V1, $shHole)) ~> K) if not E2 :: Value .
  ceq k({ shmRogue(V1, E2) } ~> K) = k({ E2 } ~> $sh3(V1, shmRogue(V1, $shHole)) ~> K) if not E2 :: Value .
  eq k({ V2 } ~> $sh3(V1, shmWrite(V1, $shHole)) ~> K) = k({ shmWrite(V1, V2) } ~> K) .
  eq k({ V2 } ~> $sh3(V1, shmSetSize(V1, $shHole)) ~> K) = k({ shmSetSize(V1, V2) } ~> K) .
  eq k({ V2 } ~> $sh3(V1, shmFill(V1, $shHole)) ~> K) = k({ shmFill(V1, V2) } ~> K) .
  eq k({ V2 } ~> $sh3(V1, shmRogue(V1, $shHole)) ~> K) = k({ shmRogue(V1, V2) } ~> K) .

  --- A temporary reference evaluates its buffer and its size as lvalues (locations).
  ceq k({ tmpref(E, Z, D) } ~> K) = k({ lvalue(E) } ~> $shTmp1(Z, D) ~> K) if not E :: Value .
   eq k({ V } ~> $shTmp1(Z, D) ~> K) = k({ tmpref(V, Z, D) } ~> K) .
  ceq k({ tmpref(V, Z, D) } ~> K) = k({ lvalue(Z) } ~> $shTmp2(V, D) ~> K) if not Z :: Value .
   eq k({ V2 } ~> $shTmp2(V, D) ~> K) = k({ tmpref(V, V2, D) } ~> K) .
  ceq k({ nullref(Z, D) } ~> K) = k({ lvalue(Z) } ~> $shNull(D) ~> K) if not Z :: Value .
   eq k({ V } ~> $shNull(D) ~> K) = k({ nullref(V, D) } ~> K) .
endfm

--- This module defines the values of shared memory, their IMP types, and the client call.
--- memref(M, D): a registered memory reference to the block M with direction D;
--- tmem(LB, LZ, D), nmem(LZ, D): a temporary memory reference to the client buffer at
---   location LB with its size at LZ, and a null one;
--- mref(O): the memory reference that the TA receives; O is the MemrefOp of the operation.

--- @kind interface
--- @feature shm
mod SHARED-MEMORY-VALUE is
  pr SHARED-MEMORY-SYNTAX .
  pr TEE-IMP-VALUE-TYPE .
  pr TEE-CLIENT-FUNC .
  pr CONFIGURATION .

  sort MrefValue .
  subsort MrefValue < Value .
  op memref : Oid MemrefDir -> Value [ctor] .
  op tmem : Nat Nat MemrefDir -> Value [ctor] .
  op nmem : Nat MemrefDir -> Value [ctor] .
  op mref : Oid -> MrefValue [ctor] .

  ops TEE-Memref TEE-SharedMem : -> ConcBType [ctor] .

  var SC : Scope .
  vars E E1 E2 ES EF Z : Exp .
  vars EL OUT : ExpList .
  var M : Oid .
  vars LB LZ : Nat .
  var D : MemrefDir .
  var MA : MemAccess .
  var V : Value .
  var K : K .

  eq k({ memrefTo(# M, D) } ~> K) = k({ memref(M, D) } ~> K) .
  eq k({ tmpref(loc(LB), loc(LZ), D) } ~> K) = k({ tmem(LB, LZ, D) } ~> K) .
  eq k({ nullref(loc(LZ), D) } ~> K) = k({ nmem(LZ, D) } ~> K) .

  --- teecInvoke runs as the stub of TEEC_InvokeCommand: its inputs are evaluated ($inH), the
  --- SMC request is sent by invoke-ta-smc, and invoke-ta-finish assigns the output values to
  --- OUT.
  eq k({ teecInvoke(ES, EF, EL, OUT) } ~> []; ~> K)
   = k($inH(argNil, (ES, EF, EL)) ~> $wait(TeecInvokeCommand) ~> $out(OUT) ~> K) .

  --- TEE_CheckMemoryAccessRights on a private buffer: the TA owns it, so it is accessible
  --- with any flags.
  ceq k({ checkMemoryAccessRights(MA, V) } ~> K) = k({ # success } ~> K) if not V :: MrefValue .

  ceq typeOfExp(SC, shmData(E)) = ty(TEE-Buffer) if typeOfExp(SC, E) = ty(TEE-Memref) .
  ceq typeOfExp(SC, shmSize(E)) = ty(int) if typeOfExp(SC, E) = ty(TEE-Memref) .
  ceq typeOfExp(SC, shmWrite(E1, E2)) = ty(void)
    if typeOfExp(SC, E1) = ty(TEE-Memref) /\ typeOfExp(SC, E2) = ty(TEE-Buffer) .
  ceq typeOfExp(SC, shmSetSize(E1, E2)) = ty(void)
    if typeOfExp(SC, E1) = ty(TEE-Memref) /\ typeOfExp(SC, E2) = ty(int) .
  ceq typeOfExp(SC, checkMemoryAccessRights(MA, E)) = ty(TEE-Result)
    if typeOfExp(SC, E) = ty(TEE-Memref) .
  ceq typeOfExp(SC, checkMemoryAccessRights(MA, E)) = ty(TEE-Result)
    if typeOfExp(SC, E) = ty(TEE-Buffer) .
  ceq typeOfExp(SC, shmAlloc(E, D)) = ty(TEE-SharedMem) if typeOfExp(SC, E) = ty(int) .
  ceq typeOfExp(SC, shmFill(E1, E2)) = ty(void)
    if typeOfExp(SC, E1) = ty(TEE-SharedMem) /\ typeOfExp(SC, E2) = ty(TEE-Buffer) .
  ceq typeOfExp(SC, shmRogue(E1, E2)) = ty(void)
    if typeOfExp(SC, E1) = ty(TEE-SharedMem) /\ typeOfExp(SC, E2) = ty(TEE-Buffer) .
  ceq typeOfExp(SC, shmView(E)) = ty(TEE-Buffer) if typeOfExp(SC, E) = ty(TEE-SharedMem) .
  ceq typeOfExp(SC, shmRetSize(E)) = ty(int) if typeOfExp(SC, E) = ty(TEE-SharedMem) .
  ceq typeOfExp(SC, shmRelease(E)) = ty(void) if typeOfExp(SC, E) = ty(TEE-SharedMem) .
  ceq typeOfExp(SC, memrefTo(E, D)) = ty(TEE-Memref) if typeOfExp(SC, E) = ty(TEE-SharedMem) .
  ceq typeOfExp(SC, tmpref(E, Z, D)) = ty(TEE-Memref)
    if E :: LExp /\ typeOfExp(SC, E) = ty(TEE-Buffer) /\ Z :: LExp /\ typeOfExp(SC, Z) = ty(int) .
  ceq typeOfExp(SC, nullref(Z, D)) = ty(TEE-Memref)
    if Z :: LExp /\ typeOfExp(SC, Z) = ty(int) .
  ceq typeOfExp(SC, teecInvoke(ES, EF, EL, OUT)) = ty(void)
    if typeOfExp(SC, ES) = ty(TEE-SessionId) /\ typeOfExp(SC, EF) = ty(TEE-CommandId) .

  --- A memory reference may be passed for a buffer parameter ([inbuf], [Internal Core] 3.4.3);
  --- it is read when the parameter is bound.  It may also be passed for an object
  --- identifier, which is an [in] parameter: the TA panics then (3.4.1).
  ceq argOk(SC, E, TEE-Buffer) = true if typeOfExp(SC, E) = ty(TEE-Memref) .
  ceq argOk(SC, E, TEE-ObjectId) = true if typeOfExp(SC, E) = ty(TEE-Memref) .
endm

--- This module defines the shared memory blocks of the clients and the memory references of
--- the operations in progress.
---   SharedMem (a block of a client, TEEC_SharedMemory):
---     owner : the client (an RA) that registered or allocated the block;
---     mem-flags : the directions the block allows (TEEC_MEM_INPUT is mrIn, TEEC_MEM_OUTPUT is
---             mrOut, both are mrInout);
---     cview : the content of the block in the client's view;
---     size  : its size, in data fragments;
---     ret-size : the size returned by the last operation (the size field of the memory
---             reference in the client's operation structure);
---     tamper : the data a rogue client may write while a reference to the block is live.
---   MemrefOp (a memory reference of an operation in progress):
---     shm : the block, or tbuf(RI, LB, LZ) and tnull(RI, LZ) for a temporary and a null
---           reference of the client RI;
---     dir : the direction of the reference;
---     size0 : the original size; size : the size the TA returns (params[i].memref.size);
---     tview : the content in the TA's view.

--- @kind state
--- @feature shm
omod SHARED-MEMORY is
  pr SHARED-MEMORY-VALUE .
  pr LIST{Data} .
  pr BASIC-DATA .

  sort DataAlts .
  op noAlt : -> DataAlts [ctor] .
  op alt : List{Data} -> DataAlts [ctor] .
  op _;;_ : DataAlts DataAlts -> DataAlts [ctor assoc comm id: noAlt] .

  class SharedMem | owner : Oid, mem-flags : MemrefDir, cview : List{Data}, size : Nat,
                    ret-size : Nat, tamper : DataAlts .
  class MemrefOp | shm : Oid, dir : MemrefDir, size0 : Nat, size : Nat, tview : List{Data} .

  --- mop(M, I): the memory reference of parameter I to M.
  op mop : Oid Nat -> Oid [ctor] .
  --- shmb(RI, N): the block that the client RI allocated with its location counter at N.
  op shmb : Oid Nat -> Oid [ctor] .
  op tbuf : Oid Nat Nat -> Oid [ctor] .
  op tnull : Oid Nat -> Oid [ctor] .
endom

--- This module defines the synchronizations of the operations, the access of a TA to its
--- memory references, and the shared memory functions of a client.

--- @kind behavior
--- @feature shm
omod SHARED-MEMORY-BEHAVIOR is
  pr SHARED-MEMORY .
  pr TRUST-APP .
  pr RICH-APP .
  pr IMP-AUX .
  pr SECURE-MONITOR-CALL .
  pr TEE-INTERNAL-CLIENT-API-BEHAVIOR .

  vars M O RI TI TK HANDLE : Oid .
  var SID : SessionId .
  var FID : APIFuncId .
  var FUNC : FuncId .
  vars VL VL' RET : ArgList .
  vars V V' : Value .
  vars D F : MemrefDir .
  vars N N0 LB LZ L : Nat .
  vars DL TL CL : List{Data} .
  var X : Data .
  var Y : Var .
  var AS : DataAlts .
  var K : K .
  var KS : KConfig .
  var MEM : Map{Nat,Value?} .
  var PVL : PVList .
  vars R W A : Bool .

  --- argLen(VL): the number of arguments of VL.
  op argLen : ArgList -> Nat .
  eq argLen(argNil) = 0 .
  eq argLen(V VL) = s(argLen(VL)) .

  --- dirOk(D, F): the direction D of a memory reference is allowed by the flags F of its
  --- block ([Client API] 3.2.5).
  op dirOk : MemrefDir MemrefDir -> Bool .
  eq dirOk(mrIn, mrIn) = true .
  eq dirOk(mrOut, mrOut) = true .
  eq dirOk(D, mrInout) = true .
  eq dirOk(mrIn, mrOut) = false .
  eq dirOk(mrOut, mrIn) = false .
  eq dirOk(mrInout, mrIn) = false .
  eq dirOk(mrInout, mrOut) = false .

  --- writable(D): the TA may write to a memory reference of direction D.
  op writable : MemrefDir -> Bool .
  eq writable(mrIn) = false .
  eq writable(mrOut) = true .
  eq writable(mrInout) = true .

  --- shmTake(N, DL): the first N fragments of DL.
  op shmTake : Nat List{Data} -> List{Data} .
  eq shmTake(0, DL) = nil .
  eq shmTake(s(N), nil) = nil .
  eq shmTake(s(N), X DL) = X shmTake(N, DL) .

  --- syncOut(D, N0, N, TL, CL): the client's data after an operation, with the reference of
  --- direction D, original size N0, final size N, the TA's view TL and the client's data CL
  --- before the operation ([Internal Core] Table 4-9).
  op syncOut : MemrefDir Nat Nat List{Data} List{Data} -> List{Data} .
  eq syncOut(mrIn, N0, N, TL, CL) = CL .
  ceq syncOut(mrOut, N0, N, TL, CL) = shmTake(N, TL) if N <= N0 .
  ceq syncOut(mrOut, N0, N, TL, CL) = CL if N0 < N .
  ceq syncOut(mrInout, N0, N, TL, CL) = shmTake(N, TL) if N <= N0 .
  ceq syncOut(mrInout, N0, N, TL, CL) = CL if N0 < N .

  --- outSize(D, N0, N): the size the client gets back.  The size of an input reference is not
  --- updated ([Client API] 3.2.5, Variable Length Return Buffers).
  op outSize : MemrefDir Nat Nat -> Nat .
  eq outSize(mrIn, N0, N) = N0 .
  eq outSize(mrOut, N0, N) = N .
  eq outSize(mrInout, N0, N) = N .

  --- accessRes(W, A, D): the result of TEE_CheckMemoryAccessRights on a memory reference of
  --- direction D, with the flags _WRITE (W) and _ANY_OWNER (A).  Without _ANY_OWNER the check
  --- fails, since the buffer is shared ([Internal Core] 4.11.1).  An input reference is not
  --- writable.
  op accessRes : Bool Bool MemrefDir -> ReturnCode .
  eq accessRes(W, false, D) = errorAccessDenied .
  eq accessRes(false, true, D) = success .
  eq accessRes(true, true, mrIn) = errorAccessDenied .
  eq accessRes(true, true, mrOut) = success .
  eq accessRes(true, true, mrInout) = success .

------------------------------------------------------------
--- Synchronization 1: the operation starts
------------------------------------------------------------

  --- shm-begin: a registered reference memref(M, D) of parameter I to a block of the client
  --- RI whose flags allow D becomes the MemrefOp mop(M, I) with the data of the block.
  ceq [shm-begin] :
    smcReq(RI, SID, FID, (VL memref(M, D) VL'))
    < M : SharedMem | owner : RI, mem-flags : F, cview : CL, size : N >
    =
    smcReq(RI, SID, FID, (VL mref(mop(M, argLen(VL))) VL'))
    < M : SharedMem | >
    < mop(M, argLen(VL)) : MemrefOp | shm : M, dir : D, size0 : N, size : N, tview : CL >
  if dirOk(D, F) .

  --- shm-begin-bad: a direction that the flags of the block do not allow is rejected by the
  --- client library with TEEC_ERROR_BAD_PARAMETERS; the operation does not reach the TEE.
  ceq [shm-begin-bad] :
    smcReq(RI, SID, FID, (VL memref(M, D) VL'))
    < M : SharedMem | owner : RI, mem-flags : F >
    =
    smcRet(RI, # errorBadParameters)
    < M : SharedMem | >
  if dirOk(D, F) = false .

  --- shm-begin-tmp, shm-begin-null: a temporary reference of the client RI takes the data and
  --- the size of its buffer; a null reference has no data and the size 0 ([Internal Core]
  --- Table 4-8).
  eq [shm-begin-tmp] :
    smcReq(RI, SID, FID, (VL tmem(LB, LZ, D) VL'))
    < RI : App | proc : (store((LB |-> # CL) ; (LZ |-> # N) ; MEM) KS) >
    =
    smcReq(RI, SID, FID, (VL mref(mop(tbuf(RI, LB, LZ), argLen(VL))) VL'))
    < RI : App | >
    < mop(tbuf(RI, LB, LZ), argLen(VL)) : MemrefOp | shm : tbuf(RI, LB, LZ), dir : D, size0 : N,
                                                      size : N, tview : CL > .
  eq [shm-begin-null] :
    smcReq(RI, SID, FID, (VL nmem(LZ, D) VL'))
    =
    smcReq(RI, SID, FID, (VL mref(mop(tnull(RI, LZ), argLen(VL))) VL'))
    < mop(tnull(RI, LZ), argLen(VL)) : MemrefOp | shm : tnull(RI, LZ), dir : D, size0 : 0,
                                                   size : 0, tview : nil > .

  --- The same for the temporary references of a TA TK that calls another TA.
  eq [shm-begin-tmp-ta] :
    (msg reqInvoke[# FUNC # (VL tmem(LB, LZ, D) VL')] from TK to HANDLE)
    < TK : App | proc : (store((LB |-> # CL) ; (LZ |-> # N) ; MEM) KS) >
    =
    (msg reqInvoke[# FUNC # (VL mref(mop(tbuf(TK, LB, LZ), argLen(VL))) VL')] from TK to HANDLE)
    < TK : App | >
    < mop(tbuf(TK, LB, LZ), argLen(VL)) : MemrefOp | shm : tbuf(TK, LB, LZ), dir : D, size0 : N,
                                                      size : N, tview : CL > .
  eq [shm-begin-null-ta] :
    (msg reqInvoke[# FUNC # (VL nmem(LZ, D) VL')] from TK to HANDLE)
    =
    (msg reqInvoke[# FUNC # (VL mref(mop(tnull(TK, LZ), argLen(VL))) VL')] from TK to HANDLE)
    < mop(tnull(TK, LZ), argLen(VL)) : MemrefOp | shm : tnull(TK, LZ), dir : D, size0 : 0,
                                                   size : 0, tview : nil > .

------------------------------------------------------------
--- Synchronization 2: the operation completes
------------------------------------------------------------

  --- shm-end: when the SMC response reaches the client RI, each MemrefOp of a block of RI is
  --- synchronized back to the block and removed.
  eq [shm-end] :
    smcRet(RI, RET)
    < O : MemrefOp | shm : M, dir : D, size0 : N0, size : N, tview : TL >
    < M : SharedMem | owner : RI, cview : CL >
    =
    smcRet(RI, RET)
    < M : SharedMem | cview : syncOut(D, N0, N, TL, CL), ret-size : outSize(D, N0, N) > .

  --- shm-end-tmp, shm-end-null: the data go back to the client buffer, and the size to the
  --- client's size variable.
  eq [shm-end-tmp] :
    smcRet(RI, RET)
    < O : MemrefOp | shm : tbuf(RI, LB, LZ), dir : D, size0 : N0, size : N, tview : TL >
    < RI : App | proc : (store((LB |-> # CL) ; (LZ |-> V) ; MEM) KS) >
    =
    smcRet(RI, RET)
    < RI : App | proc : (store((LB |-> # syncOut(D, N0, N, TL, CL)) ; (LZ |-> # outSize(D, N0, N)) ;
                               MEM) KS) > .
  eq [shm-end-null] :
    smcRet(RI, RET)
    < O : MemrefOp | shm : tnull(RI, LZ), dir : D, size0 : N0, size : N >
    < RI : App | proc : (store((LZ |-> V) ; MEM) KS) >
    =
    smcRet(RI, RET)
    < RI : App | proc : (store((LZ |-> # outSize(D, N0, N)) ; MEM) KS) > .

  --- The same for a TA TK that called another TA, when finishReqInvoke reaches it.
  eq [shm-end-tmp-ta] :
    (msg finishReqInvoke[RET] from HANDLE to TK)
    < O : MemrefOp | shm : tbuf(TK, LB, LZ), dir : D, size0 : N0, size : N, tview : TL >
    < TK : App | proc : (store((LB |-> # CL) ; (LZ |-> V) ; MEM) KS) >
    =
    (msg finishReqInvoke[RET] from HANDLE to TK)
    < TK : App | proc : (store((LB |-> # syncOut(D, N0, N, TL, CL)) ; (LZ |-> # outSize(D, N0, N)) ;
                               MEM) KS) > .
  eq [shm-end-null-ta] :
    (msg finishReqInvoke[RET] from HANDLE to TK)
    < O : MemrefOp | shm : tnull(TK, LZ), dir : D, size0 : N0, size : N >
    < TK : App | proc : (store((LZ |-> V) ; MEM) KS) >
    =
    (msg finishReqInvoke[RET] from HANDLE to TK)
    < TK : App | proc : (store((LZ |-> # outSize(D, N0, N)) ; MEM) KS) > .

------------------------------------------------------------
--- TA access
------------------------------------------------------------

  --- shm-read: the TA reads the data of a live memory reference.  This is a rule: the data
  --- may change between two reads (shm-tamper).
  rl [shm-read] :
    < TI : TrustedApp | proc : (k({ shmData(mref(O)) } ~> K) KS), status : (normal).AppStatus >
    < O : MemrefOp | tview : TL >
    =>
    < TI : TrustedApp | proc : (k({ # TL } ~> K) KS) >
    < O : MemrefOp | > .

  --- shm-size: the TA reads the size of a memory reference.
  rl [shm-size] :
    < TI : TrustedApp | proc : (k({ shmSize(mref(O)) } ~> K) KS), status : (normal).AppStatus >
    < O : MemrefOp | size : N >
    =>
    < TI : TrustedApp | proc : (k({ # N } ~> K) KS) >
    < O : MemrefOp | > .

  --- shm-write: the TA writes the data DL to an output or input-output memory reference.  The
  --- TA may write in the range of the original size ([Internal Core] 4.3.6.4).
  crl [shm-write] :
    < TI : TrustedApp | proc : (k({ shmWrite(mref(O), # DL) } ~> K) KS), status : (normal).AppStatus >
    < O : MemrefOp | dir : D, size0 : N0 >
    =>
    < TI : TrustedApp | proc : (k({ # 0 } ~> K) KS) >
    < O : MemrefOp | tview : DL >
  if writable(D) /\ size(DL) <= N0 .

  --- shm-write-input, shm-write-overflow: a write to an input memory reference, or past its
  --- original size, is a programmer error: the TA panics and its program stops.
  rl [shm-write-input] :
    < TI : TrustedApp | proc : (k({ shmWrite(mref(O), # DL) } ~> K) KS), status : (normal).AppStatus >
    < O : MemrefOp | dir : mrIn >
    =>
    < TI : TrustedApp | proc : (k(.K) KS), status : panic >
    < O : MemrefOp | > .

  crl [shm-write-overflow] :
    < TI : TrustedApp | proc : (k({ shmWrite(mref(O), # DL) } ~> K) KS), status : (normal).AppStatus >
    < O : MemrefOp | size0 : N0 >
    =>
    < TI : TrustedApp | proc : (k(.K) KS), status : panic >
    < O : MemrefOp | >
  if N0 < size(DL) .

  --- shm-set-size: the TA sets the size returned to the client.  A size larger than the
  --- original size requests a larger buffer (see syncOut).
  rl [shm-set-size] :
    < TI : TrustedApp | proc : (k({ shmSetSize(mref(O), # N) } ~> K) KS), status : (normal).AppStatus >
    < O : MemrefOp | >
    =>
    < TI : TrustedApp | proc : (k({ # 0 } ~> K) KS) >
    < O : MemrefOp | size : N > .

  --- shm-check-access: TEE_CheckMemoryAccessRights on a live memory reference.
  rl [shm-check-access] :
    < TI : TrustedApp | proc : (k({ checkMemoryAccessRights(macc(R, W, A), mref(O)) } ~> K) KS),
                        status : (normal).AppStatus >
    < O : MemrefOp | dir : D >
    =>
    < TI : TrustedApp | proc : (k({ # accessRes(W, A, D) } ~> K) KS) >
    < O : MemrefOp | > .

  --- shm-bind-buffer: a memory reference passed for a buffer parameter is read once, when the
  --- parameter is bound.  shm-bind-object-id: a memory reference passed for an object
  --- identifier ([in], [Internal Core] 3.4.1) panics the TA.
  eq [shm-bind-buffer] :
    < TI : TrustedApp | proc : (k(bind((pv(TEE-Buffer Y, mref(O)), PVL)) ~> K) KS) >
    < O : MemrefOp | tview : TL >
    =
    < TI : TrustedApp | proc : (k(bind((pv(TEE-Buffer Y, # TL), PVL)) ~> K) KS) >
    < O : MemrefOp | > .
  eq [shm-bind-object-id] :
    < TI : TrustedApp | proc : (k(bind((pv(TEE-ObjectId Y, mref(O)), PVL)) ~> K) KS),
                        status : (normal).AppStatus >
    =
    < TI : TrustedApp | proc : (k(.K) KS), status : panic > .

  --- shm-tamper: a rogue client changes the data of a live memory reference to its block to one
  --- of the alternatives of the block.
  rl [shm-tamper] :
    < O : MemrefOp | shm : M >
    < M : SharedMem | tamper : (alt(DL) ;; AS) >
    =>
    < O : MemrefOp | tview : DL >
    < M : SharedMem | > .

------------------------------------------------------------
--- Client functions
------------------------------------------------------------

  --- These are local to the client and deterministic, so they are equations (see the policy
  --- in IMP-SEMANTICS).  A block is named after the location counter, which advances.
  eq [shm-alloc] :
    < RI : RichApp | proc : (k({ shmAlloc(# N, D) } ~> K) nextLoc(L) KS) >
    =
    < RI : RichApp | proc : (k({ # shmb(RI, L) } ~> K) nextLoc(s(L)) KS) >
    < shmb(RI, L) : SharedMem | owner : RI, mem-flags : D, cview : nil, size : N, ret-size : 0,
                                tamper : noAlt > .
  eq [shm-fill] :
    < RI : RichApp | proc : (k({ shmFill(# M, # DL) } ~> K) KS) >
    < M : SharedMem | owner : RI >
    =
    < RI : RichApp | proc : (k({ # 0 } ~> K) KS) >
    < M : SharedMem | cview : DL > .
  eq [shm-view] :
    < RI : RichApp | proc : (k({ shmView(# M) } ~> K) KS) >
    < M : SharedMem | owner : RI, cview : CL >
    =
    < RI : RichApp | proc : (k({ # CL } ~> K) KS) >
    < M : SharedMem | > .
  eq [shm-ret-size] :
    < RI : RichApp | proc : (k({ shmRetSize(# M) } ~> K) KS) >
    < M : SharedMem | owner : RI, ret-size : N >
    =
    < RI : RichApp | proc : (k({ # N } ~> K) KS) >
    < M : SharedMem | > .
  eq [shm-rogue] :
    < RI : RichApp | proc : (k({ shmRogue(# M, # DL) } ~> K) KS) >
    < M : SharedMem | owner : RI, tamper : AS >
    =
    < RI : RichApp | proc : (k({ # 0 } ~> K) KS) >
    < M : SharedMem | tamper : (alt(DL) ;; AS) > .
  eq [shm-release] :
    < RI : RichApp | proc : (k({ shmRelease(# M) } ~> K) KS) >
    < M : SharedMem | owner : RI >
    =
    < RI : RichApp | proc : (k({ # 0 } ~> K) KS) > .
endom
